# Code Structure: Tests

Tests group by top-level layer but do **not** replicate every subfolder. Predictable discovery without 5-deep nesting.

## Layout

```
src/
└── adapters/
    └── telegram/
        ├── client.py
        └── formatting/
            └── formatter.py

tests/
└── adapters/
    ├── test_telegram_client.py          # not tests/adapters/telegram/test_client.py
    └── test_telegram_formatter.py
```

- Unit tests go next to the layer they exercise.
- Integration tests live in `tests/integration/` and cross layers intentionally.
- Test file names encode the subpath as a prefix (`test_telegram_client.py`) so they stay searchable.

## Good

```
tests/adapters/test_telegram_client.py
tests/adapters/test_telegram_formatter.py
tests/services/test_job_scorer.py
tests/services/test_notification_service.py
tests/integration/test_end_to_end_scoring.py
```

## Bad

```
tests/adapters/telegram/formatting/test_formatter.py   # ❌ mirrors every subfolder
tests/adapters/telegram/__init__.py                    # ❌ empty init chain
tests/adapters/telegram/test_client.py                 # ❌ same
```

Empty `__init__.py` chains, hard to browse, and you have to recreate the source structure for every test file.
